# SOC Guide for Operational Excellence

A single-page reference of recurring SOC routines for **Microsoft Defender XDR** — covering Defender for Office 365, Defender for Endpoint, Defender for Identity, and Defender for Cloud Apps.

**[→ Open the guide](./index.html)**

---

## What this is

80 routine tasks every SOC executes across the four Defender workloads, organized by:

- **Cadence** — Daily, Weekly, Monthly, Ad-hoc
- **Pattern** — Triage, Tune, Hunt, Intel, Detect, Config
- **Owner** — SecOps or SecAdmin
- **Access needed** — minimum Microsoft Entra built-in role per task

Tasks marked **Anchor** are the ones to start with for each workload and cadence — the "if you only do one thing today, do this" task.

## How to use it

- **Cards view** — scan a workload at a glance, expand any task for the deeper run-book.
- **Table view** — dense view for triaging across many tasks, with the same expandable detail.
- **Filter rail** — narrow by cadence, pattern, or owner. Combine with full-text search across task names, portals, and roles.
- **Workload tabs** — switch between Defender for Office 365, Endpoint, Identity, Cloud Apps, or All.

Every task links directly to the relevant Microsoft Defender portal page and the matching Microsoft Learn article.

## Sourcing

Task lists, portal links, and role assignments are derived from the **Microsoft SecOps guides** on Microsoft Learn:

- [Defender for Office 365 SecOps guide](https://learn.microsoft.com/defender-office-365/mdo-sec-ops-guide)
- [Defender for Endpoint daily operations](https://learn.microsoft.com/defender-endpoint/daily-operations)
- [Defender for Identity SecOps guide](https://learn.microsoft.com/defender-for-identity/sec-ops-guide)
- [Defender for Cloud Apps daily activities](https://learn.microsoft.com/defender-cloud-apps/daily-activities-to-secure-your-cloud-app-environment)

The deeper run-books on each task (steps, pitfalls, "good looks like") are author-written from those sources and from operational experience working with Defender XDR.

## A note on roles

The **Access needed** label shows the minimum Microsoft Entra built-in role required to execute the task in the Defender portal. Where a tenant has activated **Microsoft Defender XDR Unified RBAC (URBAC)**, those custom roles override Entra permissions inside the portal — see the [Defender unified RBAC permissions reference](https://learn.microsoft.com/defender-xdr/custom-permissions-details) for the equivalent mapping.

## Technical

- Single self-contained HTML file. No build step, no dependencies, no analytics.
- Works offline once loaded.
- Open `index.html` in any modern browser.

## Disclaimer

This is a personal compilation intended as a practitioner's reference. It is **not an official Microsoft asset** and is not a substitute for the canonical Microsoft Learn documentation linked above. Always validate against current Microsoft guidance for production decisions.
